ي", "approximation"], ["multi-factor model", "نموذج متعدد العوامل", "modèle multifactoriel"], ["arbitrage pricing theory", "نظرية التسعير بالمراجحة", "théorie d'évaluation par arbitrage"]], [["Item", "Answer"], ["Market risk premium", "6.0 points: 9.0 − 3.0 = 6.0."], ["Barada Wholesale", "Required 10.8 per cent, from 1.30 × 6.0 = 7.8 points on top of 3 per cent. Expected 12.0, so it is above the line and a buy."], ["Orontes Foods", "Required 8.4 per cent, from 0.90 × 6.0 = 5.4 points on top of 3 per cent. Expected 8.0, so it is marginally below the line and a sell on these figures."], ["A utility", "Required 6.0 per cent, from 0.50 × 6.0 = 3.0 points on top of 3 per cent. Expected 7.0, so it is above the line and a buy."], ["The portfolio", "Beta 0.70, from 0.5 × 0.90 = 0.45 and 0.5 × 0.50 = 0.25, so 0.45 + 0.25 = 0.70; the required return is 7.2 per cent, from 0.70 × 6.0 = 4.2 points on top of 3 per cent."], ["What it tells you", "Two of the three are mispriced on these estimates, and the one that looks dearest — the utility, on the lowest expected return — is the best buy of the three, because its risk is so low that 7.0 per cent is more than it needs to offer. Ranking by expected return alone reverses the answer."]]], "figures": {"F602-01": 0, "F602-02": 2, "F602-03": 4, "F602-04": 6, "F602-05": 8, "F602-06": 10, "F602-07": 12}, "tsec": {"0": "", "1": "", "2": "2.1", "3": "2.1", "4": "2.2", "5": "2.2", "6": "2.3", "7": "2.3", "8": "2.4", "9": "2.4", "10": "2.5", "11": "2.5", "12": "2.5"}}